{% set source_item = {} %}
{% if source and source.strip() %}
    {% set source_item = json.loads(source) %}
{% endif %}
{% set mode = "update" if source_item else "create" %}
{% set tenant = GetCustomerInfo().tenant | string %}
{% set builder_branding = "NEWO AI Employee workflow builder" if not tenant or tenant == "newo" else "AI Employee workflow builder" %}

{% set prompt %}
You are generating one `csv_outbound` canvas item for {{builder_branding}}.

<TaskMode>{{mode}}</TaskMode>
<UserRequest>
{{query}}
</UserRequest>
{% if source_item %}
<CurrentItem role="source_of_truth_for_update">
{{json.dumps(source_item, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)}}
</CurrentItem>
{% endif %}

Purpose:
- This item is saved into the `Outbound Call Campaigns (CSV)` canvas column.
- When saved with a non-empty CSV body, the platform queues outbound phone calls.

Language rules:
1. Write title and description in English by default.
2. Use another language only if <UserRequest> explicitly asks for it.
3. Do not switch language only because <UserRequest> itself is written in another language.

CSV body requirements:
1. Body must be standard CSV text, not markdown.
2. Include a header row.
3. Include a phone-number column named exactly `Phone Number`.
4. Include a call-instructions column named exactly `Reason to Call`.
5. Phone numbers must be in international format with country code, for example `+1234567890`.
6. If a field contains commas, quotes, or line breaks, escape it according to CSV rules.
7. Do not include duplicate phone numbers.
8. Do not wrap the CSV in code fences.
9. If <UserRequest> does not provide enough concrete rows to call, return an empty `body` string rather than inventing leads or phone numbers.

Title requirements:
- Use a concise batch title, for example `Outbound Call Batch`.
- Do not append `(sent)`; the save flow does that after queuing.

Description requirements:
- 1-2 concise sentences describing what the batch will do.
- If body is empty because required row data is missing, state what information is needed before calls can be queued.
{% endset %}

{% set schema = {
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "title": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Concise outbound call batch title."
    },
    "body": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Standard CSV text with Phone Number and Reason to Call columns, or empty if row data is missing."
    },
    "description": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Short business-friendly summary."
    }
  },
  "required": ["title", "body", "description"]
} %}

{% set generated_item = json.loads(structured_generation(prompt=prompt, schema=schema, thinking_budget=1020)) %}

{% set title = generated_item.title.strip() %}
{% set body = generated_item.body.strip() %}
{% set body = re.sub("^```(?:csv)?\\s*", "", body).strip() %}
{% set body = re.sub("\\s*```$", "", body).strip() %}
{% set body = re.sub("\\n{3,}", "\n", body).strip() %}
{% set description = generated_item.description.strip() %}

{% set item = {
    "title": title,
    "body": body,
    "description": description,
    "mentions": []
} %}

{{Return(val=json.dumps(item, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))}}
